The same goes for a single object.
[[get_assignment(5, all_dates=True)]] asks for something a listing does not have,
so the answer cannot stand in for the entry.
And an entry stored with such an argument would make the whole listing count as
incomplete, as we see next: the listing would be fetched again each time such a
call had been made.
<<pass a restricted request for one object through to Canvas>>=
if restricts_listing(kwargs):
  logger.info(f"Not cached: {attr_name} restricted by {kwargs}")
  return get_attr(self, *args, **kwargs)
@

Caches that already hold such a listing must recover too, and by themselves, as
a program using the library has no [[--refresh-cache]] to pass.
A listing with a restriction on any entry is not complete, so we treat it as not
fetched, and the next reader fetches it properly.

This could look like the kind of migration we otherwise solve by bumping
[[CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION]], but it is not one.
The cache file is shared between programs that each have their own copy of this
library, [[nytid]] for instance, so a copy older than this code can write such a
listing at any time.
A version bump would not stop that, and it would make programs with different
versions discard each other's cache on every run.
<<treat a listing cached with a restriction as not fetched>>=
if attr_all_fetched and any(restricts_listing(prev_kwargs)
                            for _, prev_kwargs in attr_cache.values()):
  logger.info(f"Cache invalidation: {display_plural} - cached for a subset")
  attr_all_fetched = None
@

The fetch that follows only replaces the entries Canvas returns.
A student who has left the course would keep the restriction, and the listing
would then count as incomplete on every read, at the cost of a new fetch each
time.
So we clear the restriction from what is left as well.
<<clear restrictions from entries Canvas did not return>>=
for obj_key, (obj, obj_kwargs) in list(attr_cache.items()):
  if restricts_listing(obj_kwargs):
    attr_cache[obj_key] = (obj, without_restrictions(obj_kwargs))
