We must also store the original [[get_submission]] method before decorating it,
because [[LazySubmission]] needs to call it directly to avoid double-wrapping.
We keep it on the class as well, as [[uncached_get_submission]], which is where
a [[LazySubmission]] that has been read back from the cache file finds it
(\cref{sec:lazy-submission-pickle}).
If the class already has one, the decorator has been applied before, and what
[[cls.get_submission]] holds now is our own wrapper; the method to keep is the
one we kept the first time.
Then we must decorate both [[get_submission]] and [[get_submissions]].
