A submission already in the cache was handed to some caller, who may hold it
and may have annotated it, as the listing commands do with [[user]].
A new [[LazySubmission]] in its place would leave that caller with an object
the cache no longer updates, and the next call would return one without the
annotations.
So we store what we fetched in the way the bulk fetch below does, with the
same chunk: a cached submission keeps its wrapper, which swaps in the fresh
one through [[_replace_submission]] and records the includes, and only a
submission not cached yet gets a new wrapper.
That chunk calls what was asked for [[all_includes]] and leaves the wrapper in
[[lazy_submission]].
