Asking a single submission for an include it lacks fetches it again, and the
answer must update the submission the caller already holds, not replace it in
the cache, as the prose on the single getter explains.
A caller that has annotated the submission, as the listing commands do with
[[user]], must find the annotation on what the second call returns, and that
must be the very object it holds.
